From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bastiaan van der Plaat <bastiaan.v.d.plaat@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 22:15:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add a far heap to malloc

Memory that sbrk doesn't give, like the RAM of a Memory Expansion Pak
in the GBA slot of a Nintendo DS, which ignores byte writes, becomes a
far heap with its own free list. far_malloc takes from it first and
then like malloc, which never takes from it. free and realloc put a
chunk back in the list it came from.
